056142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sQsHO","user":{"login":"HeavyBro1337","id":70683749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNjgzNzQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70683749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337","html_url":"https://github.com/HeavyBro1337","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HeavyBro1337/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T08:10:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T08:10:40Z","body":"All the hopes for Godot 4.5, I want it to be merged!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2890056142/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922146910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-2922146910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":2922146910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uLGxe","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T11:35:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T11:35:43Z","body":"Thanks for working on this! Can you explain the code changes you made to make this easier to review?\r\n\r\nIn other physics engines like Box2D we do see the accumulated impulse being used when applying the impulse in the current iteration (presumably for stability of the contacts), and we also see the inverse inertia of each body being divided by the sum of the inverse inertia of the two bodies:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/erincatto/box2d/blob/4b5e72bd44bd139fab67ad890b70e1690ff405a8/src/motor_joint.c#L215-L224\r\n\r\nIn this PR you've removed both of those elements from the calculation, which makes me skeptical that this is exactly the right approach, although the videos show that you're doing *something* right, and trying the test project on the `master` branch does show that there is *something* wrong with the current code in Godot Physics.\r\n\r\nCan you make it work while keeping those two elements? Or am I missing something else?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922146910/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924237499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-2924237499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":2924237499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uTFK7","user":{"login":"masuhajime","id":963279,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzI3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/963279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime","html_url":"https://github.com/masuhajime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T04:26:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T04:26:30Z","body":"To improve the implementation, I reviewed the code from Chipmunk2D:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/slembcke/Chipmunk2D/blob/d0239ef4599b3688a5a336373f7d0a68426414ba/src/cpRotaryLimitJoint.c\r\n- https://github.com/slembcke/Chipmunk2D/blob/d0239ef4599b3688a5a336373f7d0a68426414ba/src/cpSimpleMotor.c\r\n\r\nIn the original implementation, the calculations for both the `angular limit` and the `motor` were handled within the same if statement.\r\nI tried multiple times to keep the logic within a single if block, but I couldn’t get it to work correctly.\r\n\r\nThen, I noticed that Chipmunk2D separates the logic for the `angular limit` and the `motor` into different code paths.\r\nFollowing that approach, I decided to separate them as well. This is the most significant change in this PR.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924237499/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924289743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-2924289743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":2924289743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uTR7P","user":{"login":"masuhajime","id":963279,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzI3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/963279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime","html_url":"https://github.com/masuhajime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T04:56:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T04:56:39Z","body":"I reviewed my code again, and you're right, `j_acc` has indeed been removed.\r\nThank you for pointing that out and for sharing the relevant code from Box2D.\r\n\r\nI'd like to take some time to look into this further, including the part about inverse inertia.\r\nThis is my first time modifying physics calculations, so it's very possible that I've missed some important aspects.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924289743/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2926988746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-2926988746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":2926988746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6udk3K","user":{"login":"tomsterBG","id":117642342,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwMUZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117642342?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG","html_url":"https://github.com/tomsterBG","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomsterBG/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-01T10:30:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-01T11:01:45Z","body":"This is cool, but how can there be unit tests to prevent regression?\r\n\r\nSomething that fails right now in 4.4.1 stable and would pass if the implementation's results happen to be accurate?\r\n\r\nI'm not familiar with the headless test suite, but i'd assume we can at least have a simple scene with timer and expect certain results in a few simple scenarios and somewhat accurately time each result to ensure it doesn't go out of bounds, but not too long because currently Github builds unit tests in a few minutes already.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/43440 does not mention joints so i feel like it might not be possible, we'd have to do community testing with GDScript and perhaps GUT by bitwes if that's the case.\r\n\r\nAlso i tested it in my own project and there seems to be a massive improvement so the fix works, but as of your first commit made back in march here, i can't say it's ready as there's a bug where my cogs would teleport if they are diagonal and i suspect that it might perhaps be some division by 0 or wrapping problem as it happens at the same spot when i rotate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2926988746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2939078760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-2939078760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":2939078760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vLsho","user":{"login":"masuhajime","id":963279,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzI3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/963279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime","html_url":"https://github.com/masuhajime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T08:19:58Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T11:21:53Z","body":"@rburing\r\nThank you for the feedback.\r\n\r\nRegarding the part about \"the inverse inertia of each body being divided by the sum of the inverse inertia of the two bodies\" — I tried to keep that logic intact using the `i_sum` variable (representing the combined inverse inertia), but I wasn't able to make it work correctly while preserving the intended joint behavior. For now, I’ve excluded it from the calculation, as I couldn’t maintain stability with it in place.\r\n\r\nIf there's something I might be missing or a better way to incorporate it, I'd really appreciate it if you could take a look at the updated code.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/975ae3f0-c1d7-4660-868c-591358721e08\r\n\r\n\r\nI’ve attached a video of the current behavior. Each rope joint is limited to angular -15 to 15 degree","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2939078760/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4187475207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-4187475207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":4187475207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75l80H","user":{"login":"bored1492","id":66461796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NDYxNzk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66461796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"ht