ime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masuhajime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T00:34:38Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T00:34:38Z","body":"To those struggling with PinJoint2D angular limit issues:\r\nIf your project allows for the use of plugins, using the Rapier Godot Extension (https://godot.rapier.rs/) will resolve the issues with PinJoint2D angular limits.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4348582363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366926586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-4366926586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":4366926586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBEoC-g","user":{"login":"jauwnio","id":157239827,"node_id":"U_kgDOCV9KEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157239827?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio","html_url":"https://github.com/jauwnio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jauwnio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-03T19:02:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-03T22:34:23Z","body":"> To those struggling with PinJoint2D angular limit issues: If your project allows for the use of plugins, using the Rapier Godot Extension (https://godot.rapier.rs/) will resolve the issues with PinJoint2D angular limits.\r\n\r\nI merged your PR into my branch of Godot and it _did not_ result in proper functionality. The fish are a series of 3 rigidbodies connected by pinjoint2D (because physicalbone2D has a slew of even worse problems that make it unusable for this case)\r\n\r\nHere is with your PR:\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5288942-c2fb-4411-bcd7-f74e5937efdb\r\n\r\nAnd here is with nothing at all changed except swapped for Rapier:\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da7f080b-d2bb-411e-82c9-9d19b55c0fef\r\n\r\nI think that 2D physics have a litany of issues that need to be addressed to make it production ready for joints/bones. So I guess using Rapier is really the best workaround right now, and based on this testing, I don't think this PR fixes the problem (in my specific case)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4366926586/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4399983688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104539#issuecomment-4399983688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104539","id":4399983688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBkJsSA","user":{"login":"fracter2","id":78301601,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzAxNjAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78301601?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2","html_url":"https://github.com/fracter2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fracter2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-07T18:29:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T09:40:34Z","body":"I compiled Godot with your PR and it works for me! This fixes the issues I have been having in my personal project with ragdolls. I have not tried Rapier. \r\n\r\nWhat may be a bug (or maybe intended, I don't know) is that when a RigidBody (connected to joint) is rotated in editor, it behaves somewhat strange. Rotating the CollissionShape2D instead of the RigidBody produces the behaviour I expect.\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c9ee562-d103-44c0-846d-23f30164d47f\r\n\r\nGodot 4.6.2:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cd777a2-7f05-4f0b-908f-7db7d600ed30\r\n\r\nGodot 4.6.2 does not distinguish between rotating the RB or shape node, but then again it also doesn't correctly limit the angles anyway. The PR is also less wobbly, for some reason.\r\n\r\nMotors also work but are also notably different. Note bottom 4 arms have center of mass offset from their joints. All motors 90deg/s. This PR:\r\n<img width=\"756\" height=\"642\" alt=\"MotorsGodotPRv3\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11e8ec9a-98c7-4071-abd2-04bf68838e56\" />\r\n\r\nGodot 4.6.2:\r\n<img width=\"618\" height=\"620\" alt=\"Motorsv4 6v3\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1dbc3001-6072-4d91-abaa-510aae1711be\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nI could not find any documentation or Unit Tests that would tell me the intended behaviour for any of these scenarios. Do tell if I missed anything. Still, the PR fixes the basic use case of limiting angles, and motors feel a bit more intuitive to use. Personally I'd love to have this (or similar fix) merged.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4399983688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]